{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrackpadGestures"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A stroke runs from its first touch down to its last touch up. It goes ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"silent"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" once three fingers","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are down, before any finger has moved ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chordTravel"},{"text":" from where it landed and while no button the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"surface pressed is held (the trackpad’s press-and-hold drag), however slowly they came down and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whatever else rests on the glass. From then until the next stroke’s first touch the surfaces send","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing for it, no pointer motion, click, button or scroll (a tap’s action runs after its touch","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has ended, so silence outlasts the last lift). A two-finger scroll that a third finger joins after","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"moving is never silent and goes on as it always did; a stroke that never has three fingers down is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never silent, so one- and two-finger strokes are exactly what they were.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A silent stroke is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"armed"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", one that can become a gesture, when the three fingers that landed last","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"came down within ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chordWindow"},{"text":" of each other, before any finger moved ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chordTravel"},{"text":", with no button","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"held, no touch of the stroke cancelled and at most four fingers down. So a thumb resting on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"glass before neither keeps three fingers from arming nor becomes one of them; three fingers placed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"slowly are silent and decide nothing.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The decision comes at the first lift of one of those three (another finger lifting only leaves the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stroke), from their centroid’s net travel since arming, and their spread. A swipe when the centroid","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"travelled ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swipeDistance"},{"text":" (or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flickDistance"},{"text":" while moving at ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flickSpeed"},{"text":" over the last","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flickWindow"},{"text":"), one axis beats the other by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"axisRatio"},{"text":", and the fingers moved together: each of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the three at least ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swipeShare"},{"text":" of the centroid’s way along the swipe, and no other finger that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"moved (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chordTravel"},{"type":"text","text":" or more) that share or more against it. In a pinch or a spread some digit"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"moves against the others, however far the centroid goes (a thumb-led pinch drags it along with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the thumb). Else a pinch or a spread when the mean distance from the centroid changed by"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pinchRatio"},{"type":"text","text":", of the three and every other finger that moved (a thumb pinching with three"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fingers); else nothing. At most one decision per stroke; "},{"code":"fingers","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" counts the three and the other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fingers that moved, 4 at most. A fifth finger down leaves the stroke silent and deciding nothing;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"touches the system cancels decide nothing. So a swipe taken back before the lift does nothing, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on a Mac, and a four-finger stroke that iPadOS takes for itself (its touches cancelled) never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reaches the Mac."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pure: Foundation and CoreGraphics only, covered by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackpadGesturesTests"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Deterministic: the same touches give the same outputs. Main thread, as the touches come."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/headwireinput\/trackpadgestures"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HeadwireInput\/documentation\/HeadwireInput"]]},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:13HeadwireInput16TrackpadGesturesV","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"HeadwireInput"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TrackpadGestures","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"TrackpadGestures","roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrackpadGestures"}]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"see